  "body": "What changed:\n- The WCS page now shows the Work offset (G54-G59) control in its own group, \"Work offset (G54-G59)\".\n- The Setup page does not show the control. The group that held it is now titled \"Set WCS from features\", because only that row stays in it.\n- The control keeps its command, `SetSetupWorkOffset`, and the setup's own slot (`setup::wcs_slot`). Undo and redo do not change. No second derivation of G54-G59 exists.\n\nPinning tests (structural, in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/`):\n- `one_wcs::the_work_offset_control_is_on_the_wcs_page_and_not_the_setup_page`\n- `one_wcs::the_wcs_page_shows_the_work_offset_dropdown_and_no_setups_page_pointer` (the group sits under the origin group)\n- `setup_settings_page::the_setup_page_is_laid_out_in_groups_like_the_wcs_page` (no work offset row on the Setup page)\n- `structural` Settings page test (zero work offset combos)\n\nQuick gate: green (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`). Clippy on `camcraft-ui`: clean. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\nNot exercised: no screenshot exists, because the GUI was not started. The \"Set WCS from features\" row stays on the Setup page (see `docs/decisions/1648-wcs-page-work-offset.md`).\n\nChangelog: UI: the Work offset (G54-G59) control moves from the Setup page to the WCS page.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1648\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
